IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `ea-part2`
IMPORT `ea-part2-continuity`
IMPORT `ea-part3-salary`
IMPORT `ea-part4-hours`
IMPORT `ea-parts5to8`
IMPORT `ea-part9-maternity`
IMPORT `ea-part10-leave`
IMPORT `ea-part12-records`
IMPORT `ea-part12-retrenchment`
IMPORT `ea-retrenchment-reporting-notification`
IMPORT `ea-seat`
IMPORT `ea-seat-employer`

-- Employment Act 1968 -- the employer's seat layer, worked cases.
--
-- SEAT: the employer. Importing ea-seat.l4 and ea-seat-employer.l4 together
-- is itself the first test: the two layers define no name twice.
--
-- Every expected value is worked by hand from the text, and written beside the
-- assertion. MIRROR cases ask the same facts from both seats and assert that
-- each seat gives the same, hand-worked answer: for a yes/no question both are
-- asserted true (or both false); for a number both are asserted equal to it.

§ `Fixtures`

GIVEN `w26` IS A BOOLEAN, `y2` IS A BOOLEAN, `y5` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A ServiceLength
DECIDE `service` `w26` `y2` `y5` IS
    ServiceLength WITH
        `employed for 26 weeks or more` IS `w26`
        `employed for 2 years or more` IS `y2`
        `employed for 5 years or more` IS `y5`

`a new starter` MEANS `service` FALSE FALSE FALSE
`three years in` MEANS `service` TRUE TRUE FALSE
`ten years in` MEANS `service` TRUE TRUE TRUE

GIVEN `provides` IS A BOOLEAN, `days` IS A NUMBER, `symmetrical` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A ContractTerms
DECIDE `terms` `provides` `days` `symmetrical` IS
    ContractTerms WITH
        `the contract makes provision for notice` IS `provides`
        `the notice period the contract provides, in days` IS `days`
        `the contract provides the same length for both parties` IS `symmetrical`

`a silent contract` MEANS `terms` FALSE 0 TRUE
`a generous contract of 60 days` MEANS `terms` TRUE 60 TRUE
`a mean contract of 1 day` MEANS `terms` TRUE 1 TRUE

GIVEN `written` IS A BOOLEAN, `days` IS A NUMBER, `waived` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A Notice
DECIDE `a notice given` `written` `days` `waived` IS
    Notice WITH
        `the notice is in writing` IS `written`
        `the length given, in days` IS `days`
        `the receiving party waived the right to notice` IS `waived`

GIVEN `days` IS A NUMBER, `leave` IS A BOOLEAN, `excuse` IS A BOOLEAN, `informed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH AN Absence
DECIDE `an absence of` `days` `leave` `excuse` `informed` IS
    Absence WITH
        `days absent continuously` IS `days`
        `with prior leave from the employer` IS `leave`
        `the employee has a reasonable excuse for the absence` IS `excuse`
        `the employee informed or attempted to inform the employer of the excuse` IS `informed`

GIVEN `immediate` IS A BOOLEAN, `undertook the risk` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DangerFacts
DECIDE `danger that is` `immediate` `undertook the risk` IS
    DangerFacts WITH
        `the threat is to the employee or the employee's dependant` IS TRUE
        `the danger is immediate` IS `immediate`
        `the danger is to the person` IS TRUE
        `the danger is by violence or disease` IS TRUE
        `the employee undertook by the contract of service to run that risk` IS `undertook the risk`

GIVEN `misconduct` IS A BOOLEAN, `inquiry` IS A BOOLEAN, `suspended` IS A BOOLEAN, `days` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DismissalFacts
DECIDE `dismissal facts` `misconduct` `inquiry` `suspended` `days` IS
    DismissalFacts WITH
        `there was misconduct inconsistent with the conditions of service` IS `misconduct`
        `the employer held a due inquiry` IS `inquiry`
        `the employee was instead down-graded` IS FALSE
        `the employee was instead suspended without salary` IS `suspended`
        `the days of suspension` IS `days`

GIVEN `manager` IS A BOOLEAN, `with notice` IS A BOOLEAN, `in lieu` IS A BOOLEAN, `six months` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A Dismissed
DECIDE `a dismissed employee` `manager` `with notice` `in lieu` `six months` IS
    Dismissed WITH
        `in a managerial or an executive position` IS `manager`
        `dismissed with notice` IS `with notice`
        `dismissed without notice but paid salary in lieu` IS `in lieu`
        `served that employer for at least 6 months in any position` IS `six months`

GIVEN `years` IS A NUMBER, `redundancy` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A ServiceForBenefits
DECIDE `service for benefits` `years` `redundancy` IS
    ServiceForBenefits WITH
        `years of continuous service with the employer` IS `years`
        `dismissed on the ground of redundancy or by reason of a reorganisation` IS `redundancy`
        `the service has ceased` IS TRUE

GIVEN `workman` IS A BOOLEAN, `manager` IS A BOOLEAN, `salary` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A Worker
DECIDE `a worker` `workman` `manager` `salary` IS
    Worker WITH
        `is a workman` IS `workman`
        `is employed in a managerial or an executive position` IS `manager`
        `monthly salary excluding overtime, bonus, annual wage supplement, productivity incentive and allowances` IS `salary`

GIVEN `age` IS A NUMBER, `industrial` IS A BOOLEAN, `family only` IS A BOOLEAN, `light work` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A YoungWorker
DECIDE `a young worker` `age` `industrial` `family only` `light work` IS
    YoungWorker WITH
        `age in completed years` IS `age`
        `employed in an industrial undertaking` IS `industrial`
        `employed in a non-industrial undertaking` IS NOT `industrial`
        `the industrial undertaking employs only members of the same family` IS `family only`
        `the work is light work suited to the child's capacity` IS `light work`
        `a medical officer has certified the work suited to the child's capacity` IS FALSE
        `the Minister has declared this an industrial undertaking in which a young person must not be employed` IS FALSE

GIVEN `transferred` IS A BOOLEAN, `worked in it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH AN EmployerChange
DECIDE `a change of employer` `transferred` `worked in it` IS
    EmployerChange WITH
        `a body corporate was substituted as employer by or under written law` IS FALSE
        `the employer died and the employee was taken into the employment of the personal representatives or trustees` IS FALSE
        `there was a change in the partners, personal representatives or trustees who employ the person` IS FALSE
        `an undertaking or part of one was transferred from one person to another` IS `transferred`
        `the employee was employed by the transferor in the undertaking or part transferred` IS `worked in it`

GIVEN `monthly rate` IS A NUMBER, `full required` IS A NUMBER, `short required` IS A NUMBER, `full worked` IS A NUMBER, `short worked` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH AN IncompleteMonth
DECIDE `an incomplete month` `monthly rate` `full required` `short required` `full worked` `short worked` IS
    IncompleteMonth WITH
        `the employee is monthly-rated` IS TRUE
        `commenced employment after the first day of the month` IS TRUE
        `employment was terminated before the end of the month` IS FALSE
        `took leave of absence without pay for one or more days` IS FALSE
        `took leave of absence to perform national service under the Enlistment Act 1970` IS FALSE
        `the monthly gross rate of pay` IS `monthly rate`
        `full days the employee is required to work in that month` IS `full required`
        `short days the employee is required to work in that month, of 5 hours or less` IS `short required`
        `full days actually worked` IS `full worked`
        `short days actually worked, of 5 hours or less` IS `short worked`

`consent given and standing` MEANS Consent WITH `written consent was given` IS TRUE, `written notice of withdrawal was given before the deduction was made` IS FALSE
`consent given then withdrawn` MEANS Consent WITH `written consent was given` IS TRUE, `written notice of withdrawal was given before the deduction was made` IS TRUE
`no consent` MEANS Consent WITH `written consent was given` IS FALSE, `written notice of withdrawal was given before the deduction was made` IS FALSE

GIVEN `proposed` IS A NUMBER, `loss` IS A NUMBER, `permitted` IS A BOOLEAN, `showed cause` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DamagesDeduction
DECIDE `a damages deduction` `proposed` `loss` `permitted` `showed cause` IS
    DamagesDeduction WITH
        `the amount of the damages or loss caused by the employee's neglect or default` IS `loss`
        `one month's wages` IS 2000
        `the amount the employer proposes to deduct` IS `proposed`
        `the Commissioner has permitted a larger deduction` IS `permitted`
        `the employee has been given an opportunity of showing cause` IS `showed cause`

GIVEN `whole day` IS A BOOLEAN, `shift work` IS A BOOLEAN, `thirty hours` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A RestDayArrangement
DECIDE `a rest day arrangement` `whole day` `shift work` `thirty hours` IS
    RestDayArrangement WITH
        `a rest day of one whole day was allowed in the week` IS `whole day`
        `the employee is engaged in shift work` IS `shift work`
        `a continuous period of 30 hours was substituted` IS `thirty hours`
        `the substituted period commenced before 6 p.m. on a Sunday` IS FALSE
        `the employer determines the rest day` IS FALSE
        `a roster was prepared before the commencement of the month` IS FALSE

GIVEN `hours` IS A NUMBER, `own request` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A RestDayWork
DECIDE `rest day work` `hours` `own request` IS
    RestDayWork WITH
        `hours agreed as the usual hours of work per day were agreed` IS FALSE
        `the agreed usual hours of work per day` IS 0
        `the hours actually worked on the rest day` IS `hours`
        `the basic rate of pay for one day's work` IS 100
        `the hourly basic rate of pay` IS 12.5
        `the work was at the employee's own request` IS `own request`

GIVEN `five day week` IS A BOOLEAN, `day hours` IS A NUMBER, `consecutive` IS A NUMBER, `monthly overtime` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A HoursWorked
DECIDE `hours worked` `five day week` `day hours` `consecutive` `monthly overtime` IS
    HoursWorked WITH
        `the pattern` IS WorkPattern WITH
            `by agreement, hours on one or more days of the week are less than 8` IS FALSE
            `by agreement, the employee works not more than 5 days a week` IS `five day week`
            `by agreement, hours in every alternate week are less than 44` IS FALSE
        `hours worked in the day` IS `day hours`
        `hours worked in the week` IS 44
        `hours worked in the continuous period of 2 weeks` IS 88
        `consecutive hours worked without a period of leisure` IS `consecutive`
        `the hourly basic rate of pay` IS 12.5
        `overtime hours worked in the month` IS `monthly overtime`
        `a section 38(2) circumstance applies` IS FALSE

GIVEN `unpaid leave` IS A BOOLEAN, `non-working day` IS A BOOLEAN, `day off given` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A PublicHolidayFacts
DECIDE `a public holiday` `unpaid leave` `non-working day` `day off given` IS
    PublicHolidayFacts WITH
        `the day is a public holiday falling during the employment` IS TRUE
        `another day was substituted by agreement` IS FALSE
        `the public holiday falls on a rest day` IS FALSE
        `the public holiday falls on a day the employee is not required to work` IS `non-working day`
        `the employee is on leave of absence without pay granted at the employee's request` IS `unpaid leave`
        `the employer gave a day off in substitution` IS `day off given`

GIVEN `months total` IS A NUMBER, `years` IS A NUMBER, `months in year` IS A NUMBER, `absent` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A LeaveService
DECIDE `leave service` `months total` `years` `months in year` `absent` IS
    LeaveService WITH
        `completed months of service with the employer` IS `months total`
        `completed 12 month periods of continuous service` IS `years`
        `completed months of service in that year` IS `months in year`
        `absent without permission or reasonable excuse for more than 20% of the working days` IS `absent`

GIVEN `months` IS A NUMBER, `examined` IS A BOOLEAN, `hospital` IS A BOOLEAN, `hosp days` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A SickLeaveFacts
DECIDE `sick facts` `months` `examined` `hospital` `hosp days` IS
    SickLeaveFacts WITH
        `completed months of service with the employer` IS `months`
        `examined by a medical practitioner` IS `examined`
        `hospitalisation is necessary` IS `hospital`
        `days on which the employee is hospitalised` IS `hosp days`

GIVEN `arrangement` IS AN AbsenceArrangement, `months` IS A NUMBER, `daily` IS A NUMBER, `other employer` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MaternityFacts
DECIDE `maternity facts` `arrangement` `months` `daily` `other employer` IS
    MaternityFacts WITH
        `the arrangement` IS `arrangement`
        `delivered on or after 22 August 2015, or with an estimated delivery date on or after that day` IS TRUE
        `months served preceding the day of confinement` IS `months`
        `the gross rate of pay for one day` IS `daily`
        `days worked during the benefit period before confinement` IS 0
        `has worked for another employer after absenting herself under this Part` IS `other employer`

GIVEN `incomplete` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH AN EmployeeRecord
DECIDE `an employee record` `incomplete` IS
    EmployeeRecord WITH
        `the person is an employee or a former employee of the employer` IS TRUE
        `a record was made` IS TRUE
        `the record contains the prescribed particulars` IS TRUE
        `the record has been kept throughout the prescribed record retention period` IS TRUE
        `the record is readily accessible to the employee or former employee` IS TRUE
        `the record is incomplete or inaccurate` IS `incomplete`
        `the employer knew it was incomplete or inaccurate` IS FALSE

GIVEN `termination sum paid` IS A BOOLEAN, `termination slip given` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A PaySlipFacts
DECIDE `pay slips` `termination sum paid` `termination slip given` IS
    PaySlipFacts WITH
        `a pay slip was given for the salary period` IS TRUE
        `a pay slip was given for a sum paid under section 22 or 23` IS `termination slip given`
        `a sum was paid under section 22 or 23` IS `termination sum paid`
        `given within the time prescribed` IS TRUE
        `in the prescribed form and containing the prescribed information` IS TRUE
        `given as an electronic record accessible and useable for subsequent reference` IS FALSE
        `the pay slip is incomplete or inaccurate` IS FALSE
        `the employer is exempted by an order under section 96(5)` IS FALSE

GIVEN `after 2016` IS A BOOLEAN, `given` IS A BOOLEAN, `days` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A KeyTermsFacts
DECIDE `key terms` `after 2016` `given` `days` IS
    KeyTermsFacts WITH
        `the contract of service was entered into on or after 1 April 2016` IS `after 2016`
        `employed for a period not shorter than the prescribed minimum period of service` IS TRUE
        `a written record of the key employment terms was given` IS `given`
        `days after the start of employment when it was given` IS `days`
        `another period has been prescribed in substitution` IS FALSE
        `the substituted period in days` IS 0

GIVEN `workforce` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `Notice of retrenchment`
DECIDE `a redundancy notice with a workforce of` `workforce` IS
    `Notice of retrenchment` WITH
        `the person is an employee under section 2(1) of the Act` IS TRUE
        `the contract` IS `Contract of service` WITH
            `specifies an end date` IS FALSE
            `term of employment in months` IS 0
        `employees within the Notification on the day notice is given` IS `workforce`
        `the employer initiated the termination` IS TRUE
        `the reason is redundancy or a reorganisation` IS TRUE
        `the day the notice is given` IS 1806
        `the day the notice takes effect` IS 1837

§ `Whom the Act covers`

-- s 2(1): works under a contract of service, not a seafarer or domestic worker.
#ASSERT `As the employer, is this person an employee under the Act` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE

-- MIRROR. s 35(a): a workman at exactly $4,500 is covered by Part 4.
#ASSERT (`As the employer, must I apply Part 4 to this employee` (`a worker` TRUE FALSE 4500) `the caps as the Act states them`) AND (`Do the rest day, hours and overtime rules cover me` (`a worker` TRUE FALSE 4500) `the caps as the Act states them`)
-- MIRROR. A manager or executive is outside s 35(b) at any salary.
#ASSERT (NOT (`As the employer, must I apply Part 4 to this employee` (`a worker` FALSE TRUE 1000) `the caps as the Act states them`)) AND (NOT (`Do the rest day, hours and overtime rules cover me` (`a worker` FALSE TRUE 1000) `the caps as the Act states them`))

-- s 68(3): light work in a non-industrial undertaking needs the child to be 13.
-- At 12 no exception applies, so employing the child breaks s 68(1).
#ASSERT `As the employer, would employing this child break the Act` (`a young worker` 12 FALSE FALSE TRUE)
-- At 13, the same light work is permitted.
#ASSERT (NOT (`As the employer, would employing this child break the Act` (`a young worker` 13 FALSE FALSE TRUE)))

§ `Notice, and ending the contract`

-- MIRROR. ss 8, 10(3)(d): the contract's 1 day is void for a ten-year
-- employee; 4 weeks = 28 days, the same for both sides.
#ASSERT (`As the employer, how many days of notice must I give` `a mean contract of 1 day` `ten years in` EQUALS 28) AND (`How many days of notice am I owed` `a mean contract of 1 day` `ten years in` EQUALS 28)

-- MIRROR. s 11(1): $200 a day for the 28 days that govern = $5,600.
#ASSERT (`As the employer, how much must I pay in lieu of notice` 200 `a mean contract of 1 day` `ten years in` EQUALS 5600) AND (`How much must I be paid in lieu of notice` 200 `a mean contract of 1 day` `ten years in` EQUALS 5600)

-- s 10(5): the day of giving counts. 14 written days meets the 14 that govern.
#ASSERT `As the employer, is the notice I have given long enough` (`a notice given` TRUE 14 FALSE) `a silent contract` `three years in`
-- 13 days does not.
#ASSERT (NOT (`As the employer, is the notice I have given long enough` (`a notice given` TRUE 13 FALSE) `a silent contract` `three years in`))

-- s 11(2): wilful breach of a condition -- no notice, no payment.
#ASSERT `As the employer, may I end the contract without notice for the employee's wilful breach` TRUE

-- MIRROR. s 13(2): 3 days in a row, no leave, no excuse, not told -- deemed
-- broken, on both seats.
#ASSERT (`As the employer, is my employee treated as having broken the contract by being absent` (`an absence of` 3 FALSE FALSE FALSE)) AND (`Am I treated as having broken my contract by being absent` (`an absence of` 3 FALSE FALSE FALSE))

-- s 13(1): failing to pay salary under Part 3 is the employer's deemed breach.
#ASSERT `As the employer, am I treated as having broken the contract by not paying salary` TRUE

-- MIRROR. s 15: immediate danger by violence or disease, not undertaken.
#ASSERT (`As the employer, may my employee leave without notice because of danger` (`danger that is` TRUE FALSE)) AND (`May I leave without notice because of danger` (`danger that is` TRUE FALSE))

§ `Dismissal and suspension`

-- MIRROR. s 14(1): misconduct and a due inquiry.
#ASSERT (`As the employer, may I dismiss without notice for misconduct` (`dismissal facts` TRUE TRUE FALSE 0)) AND (`Can my employer dismiss me without notice for misconduct` (`dismissal facts` TRUE TRUE FALSE 0))

-- MIRROR. s 14(1)(b): one week (7 days) is the most.
#ASSERT (`As the employer, may I suspend without pay` (`dismissal facts` TRUE TRUE TRUE 7)) AND (`Is my suspension without pay lawful` (`dismissal facts` TRUE TRUE TRUE 7))
-- 8 days is over the week.
#ASSERT (NOT (`As the employer, may I suspend without pay` (`dismissal facts` TRUE TRUE TRUE 8)))

-- MIRROR. s 14(2A)(a): a manager dismissed with notice before 6 months'
-- service may not claim, on either seat.
#ASSERT (NOT (`As the employer, can the employee I dismissed claim for wrongful dismissal` (`a dismissed employee` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE))) AND (NOT (`Can I claim for wrongful dismissal` (`a dismissed employee` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE)))

-- s 18A(1): the undertaking the employee worked in was transferred.
#ASSERT `As the employer, is the employee's service continuous across the change of employer` (`a change of employer` TRUE TRUE)
-- Transferred, but the employee did not work in the part transferred.
#ASSERT (NOT (`As the employer, is the employee's service continuous across the change of employer` (`a change of employer` TRUE FALSE)))

§ `Paying salary`

-- s 21(2): overtime within 14 days of the end of the salary period.
#ASSERT `As the employer, how many days do I have to pay` `additional payment for overtime work` EQUALS 14

-- MIRROR. s 22: paying 4 days after a dismissal is late, on both seats.
#ASSERT (`As the employer, did I pay late` `dismissal by the employer` 4) AND (`Was I paid late` `dismissal by the employer` 4)

-- s 20A: $2,400 a month; required 22 full + 4 short days = 24; worked 10 full
-- + 2 short = 11. 2400 / 24 x 11 = $1,100.
#ASSERT `As the employer, how much salary must I pay for an incomplete month` (`an incomplete month` 2400 22 4 10 2) EQUALS 1100

§ `Deductions from salary`

-- MIRROR. s 27(1A): accommodation needs written consent, and withdrawn consent
-- does not stand.
#ASSERT (NOT (`As the employer, may I make this deduction` `house accommodation supplied by the employer` `consent given then withdrawn`)) AND (NOT (`Can my employer make this deduction from my salary` `house accommodation supplied by the employer` `consent given then withdrawn`))
-- MIRROR. s 27(1)(a): absence needs no consent.
#ASSERT (`As the employer, may I make this deduction` `absence from work` `no consent`) AND (`Can my employer make this deduction from my salary` `absence from work` `no consent`)

-- MIRROR. s 29: $400 of a $900 loss, wages $2,000 (a quarter is $500), cause
-- shown.
#ASSERT (`As the employer, may I deduct this amount for damage or loss` (`a damages deduction` 400 900 FALSE TRUE) `the proportions as the Act states them`) AND (`Can my employer deduct this amount for damage or loss I caused` (`a damages deduction` 400 900 FALSE TRUE) `the proportions as the Act states them`)
-- $600 is over the quarter ($500) without the Commissioner's permission.
#ASSERT (NOT (`As the employer, may I deduct this amount for damage or loss` (`a damages deduction` 600 900 FALSE TRUE) `the proportions as the Act states them`))

-- s 28(2): $2,000 for the period, absent 5 of 20 days: 2000 x 5/20 = $500.
#ASSERT `As the employer, what is the most I may deduct for absence` 2000 5 20 EQUALS 500

-- s 30(2): $520 of accommodation on a $2,000 salary is over a quarter ($500),
-- even though the value supplied is $600.
#ASSERT (NOT (`As the employer, are my accommodation deductions within the limits` 520 600 2000 `the proportions as the Act states them`))

-- s 32(1): $1,100 of countable deductions on $2,000 is over 50% ($1,000).
#ASSERT (NOT (`As the employer, are my deductions within the 50% cap` 1100 2000 FALSE `the proportions as the Act states them`))
-- s 32(2): the cap does not apply to the last salary on termination.
#ASSERT `As the employer, are my deductions within the 50% cap` 1100 2000 TRUE `the proportions as the Act states them`

§ `Rest days, hours and overtime`

-- s 36(2): a shift worker's continuous 30 hours counts as the rest day.
#ASSERT `As the employer, have I allowed a rest day this week` (`a rest day arrangement` FALSE TRUE TRUE)

-- MIRROR. s 37(2)(a): 4 hours at the employee's request, normal hours deemed 8:
-- not more than half, so half a day's pay = $50.
#ASSERT (`As the employer, what must I pay for rest day work` (`rest day work` 4 TRUE) EQUALS 50) AND (`What must I be paid for working on my rest day` (`rest day work` 4 TRUE) EQUALS 50)
-- s 37(3)(c): 10 hours at the employer's request: two days' pay ($200) plus
-- 2 excess hours x $12.50 x 1.5 ($37.50) = $237.50.
#ASSERT (`As the employer, what must I pay for rest day work` (`rest day work` 10 FALSE) EQUALS 237.5) AND (`What must I be paid for working on my rest day` (`rest day work` 10 FALSE) EQUALS 237.5)

-- MIRROR. s 38(4): 2 hours x $12.50 x 1.5 = $37.50.
#ASSERT (`As the employer, how much overtime must I pay` 2 12.5 EQUALS 37.5) AND (`What is my overtime pay` 2 12.5 EQUALS 37.5)

-- s 38(1)(b): 10 hours in a day, ordinary pattern, limit 8: 2 hours overtime.
#ASSERT `As the employer, how many hours today attract overtime` (`hours worked` FALSE 10 5 0) EQUALS 2

-- s 38(1)(a): 7 hours in a row without a break is more than 6.
#ASSERT `As the employer, have I broken the 6 consecutive hours rule` (`hours worked` FALSE 8 7 0)

-- s 38(5): 73 hours of overtime in the month is over 72.
#ASSERT `As the employer, have I broken the 72 hour overtime limit` (`hours worked` FALSE 8 5 73)

§ `Holidays and leave`

-- s 88(1): a public holiday during the employment is a paid holiday.
#ASSERT `As the employer, must I give a paid holiday` (`a public holiday` FALSE FALSE FALSE)
-- s 88(2): not during unpaid leave taken at the employee's request.
#ASSERT (NOT (`As the employer, must I give a paid holiday` (`a public holiday` TRUE FALSE FALSE)))

-- MIRROR. s 88A(1)(a): a full first year: 7 days.
#ASSERT (`As the employer, how many days of annual leave must I give` (`leave service` 12 1 12 FALSE) EQUALS 7) AND (`How many days of annual leave do I get` (`leave service` 12 1 12 FALSE) EQUALS 7)

-- MIRROR. s 89(2): 6 months' service, hospitalised 10 days: lesser of 60 and
-- 14 + 10 = 24.
#ASSERT (`As the employer, how many days of paid sick leave must I allow` (`sick facts` 6 TRUE TRUE 10) EQUALS 24) AND (`How many days of paid sick leave can I take` (`sick facts` 6 TRUE TRUE 10) EQUALS 24)

-- MIRROR. s 45: 1.5 years' service, dismissed for redundancy: barred.
#ASSERT (`As the employer, does short service bar a retrenchment benefit` (`service for benefits` 1.5 TRUE)) AND (`Am I barred from a retrenchment benefit by my short service` (`service for benefits` 1.5 TRUE))

§ `Maternity`

-- MIRROR. s 76(2B): 3 months' service before confinement qualifies.
#ASSERT (`As the employer, must I pay during the maternity benefit period` (`maternity facts` `the default -- 4 weeks before and 8 weeks after` 3 100 FALSE)) AND (`Am I entitled to be paid during my maternity benefit period` (`maternity facts` `the default -- 4 weeks before and 8 weeks after` 3 100 FALSE))
-- MIRROR. s 83: working for another employer during the absence forfeits it.
#ASSERT (NOT (`As the employer, must I pay during the maternity benefit period` (`maternity facts` `the default -- 4 weeks before and 8 weeks after` 12 100 TRUE))) AND (NOT (`Am I entitled to be paid during my maternity benefit period` (`maternity facts` `the default -- 4 weeks before and 8 weeks after` 12 100 TRUE)))

-- MIRROR. s 76(1A)(a): 8 weeks x 7 days x $100 = $5,600.
#ASSERT (`As the employer, how much maternity pay must I pay` (`maternity facts` `the default -- 4 weeks before and 8 weeks after` 3 100 FALSE) EQUALS 5600) AND (`How much maternity pay do I get` (`maternity facts` `the default -- 4 weeks before and 8 weeks after` 3 100 FALSE) EQUALS 5600)

-- MIRROR. s 81: notice given before the absence that would expire during it.
#ASSERT (`As the employer, would my notice of dismissal during her maternity absence be unlawful` TRUE FALSE TRUE) AND (`Is the notice of dismissal I was given during my maternity absence unlawful` TRUE FALSE TRUE)

-- s 82: knowingly employing her in the 4 weeks after confinement.
#ASSERT `As the employer, am I guilty of the section 82 offence` TRUE TRUE

§ `Records, key employment terms and pay slips`

-- s 95(3): an incomplete record is a failure, though the employer did not know.
#ASSERT (NOT (`As the employer, have I kept the employee record as required` (`an employee record` TRUE)))

-- MIRROR. s 95A(2): given on day 15, past the 14 days.
#ASSERT (`As the employer, have I failed to give the key employment terms in time` (`key terms` TRUE TRUE 15)) AND (`Has my employer failed to give me my key employment terms in time` (`key terms` TRUE TRUE 15))

-- s 96(1): every pay slip given in time, form and full, no termination sum.
#ASSERT `As the employer, have I met the pay slip duty` (`pay slips` FALSE FALSE)
-- s 96(1)(b): a sum paid on dismissal needs its own pay slip.
#ASSERT (NOT (`As the employer, have I met the pay slip duty` (`pay slips` TRUE FALSE)))

§ `Retrenchment reporting`

-- MIRROR. Notification paras 2, 3: 40 covered employees, an open-ended
-- contract, retrenched for redundancy: the report is due.
#ASSERT (`As the employer, must I report this retrenchment` (`a redundancy notice with a workforce of` 40)) AND (`Must my employer report my retrenchment to the Commissioner` (`a redundancy notice with a workforce of` 40))
-- MIRROR. Para 2(1): 9 covered employees is under 10.
#ASSERT (NOT (`As the employer, must I report this retrenchment` (`a redundancy notice with a workforce of` 9))) AND (NOT (`Must my employer report my retrenchment to the Commissioner` (`a redundancy notice with a workforce of` 9)))

-- Para 4: notice on day 0 (Monday 1 November 2021). Working days 1-4 are Tue
-- to Fri, 5 and 6 are the weekend, day 7 (Monday) is the 5th working day.
#ASSERT `As the employer, what is the last day for my retrenchment report` 0 (LIST) EQUALS 7
-- With a public holiday on day 2, the 5th working day is day 8.
#ASSERT `As the employer, what is the last day for my retrenchment report` 0 (LIST 2) EQUALS 8

-- s 96A(2): 12 notices needing a report, all 12 properly reported.
#ASSERT `As the employer, have I complied with retrenchment reporting` 40 12 12

§ `What I can be penalised for`

-- ss 126A(aa), 126B(1)(aa): 2 employees not properly reported, at a supplied
-- prescribed amount of $1,000 each: at most $2,000.
#ASSERT `As the employer, what is the most my retrenchment reporting penalties could total` 40 12 10 1000 EQUALS 2000

-- s 126D(2): a direction not complied with, no reasonable excuse.
#ASSERT `As the employer, have I committed the section 126D(2) offence` TRUE TRUE FALSE

-- s 126D(2): fine up to $5,000, imprisonment up to 6 months.
#ASSERT `As the employer, what is the most I can be fined for disobeying a direction` EQUALS 5000
#ASSERT `As the employer, what is the longest I can be imprisoned for disobeying a direction` EQUALS 6
